     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-04 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Akhilesh Yadav Calls for Unity Ahead of Rajya Sabha Polls</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Samajwadi Party chief Akhilesh Yadav urged political unity for the upcoming Rajya Sabha elections, stating it is a time to move past earlier grievances. His remarks follow reports that the party intends to field three candidates for the 10 available seats in Uttar Pradesh, a move that could trigger cross-voting. The party has already nominated Ram Gopal Yadav and Reliance executive Dhanraj Parimal Nathwani.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-04/akhilesh-yadav-calls-for-unity-ahead-of-rajya-sabha-polls.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>While the BJP-led alliance is positioned to win seven seats, the Samajwadi Party hopes to secure two with Congress support. SP members have claimed several BJP MLAs are interested in switching parties, setting the stage for a competitive election cycle.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately captures the political context of the Rajya Sabha elections and Akhilesh Yadav's remarks.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/rajya-sabha-elections-time-for-coming-together-akhilesh-yadav/article71536816.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
