       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · ESPN Cricinfo · 2026-10-04 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Dogra and Nasir Lead Jammu &amp; Kashmir to Irani Cup Advantage</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#cricket</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Jammu &amp; Kashmir secured a first-innings lead of 41 runs against the Rest of India during their Irani Cup match in Srinagar. Despite struggling at 166 for 8, the team recovered thanks to a late-innings rearguard effort.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-04/dogra-and-nasir-lead-jammu-kashmir-to-irani-cup-advantage.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Lone Nasir, batting at number 10, contributed a vital 64 off 58 balls to bolster the total. The match, played on a pitch favoring fast bowlers, saw the Rest of India bowled out for 237 in their first innings. The performance marked a significant turnaround for the Jammu &amp; Kashmir side after their early batting collapse.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is concise, accurate, and captures the key sporting details provided in the source summary.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.cricinfo.com/ci/content/story/1556925.html?ex_cid=OTC-RSS" rel="noopener">ESPN Cricinfo</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
