     <article class="story single" data-beat="entertainment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · TOI Entertainment · 2026-10-04 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge conf" title="Reported by TOI Entertainment, Bollywood Hungama">confirmed by 2 sources</span></div>
       <h1>'Hanuman Ansh' Sets Worldwide Telugu Release for October 9, 2026</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Entertainment</span> <span>#Film Release</span> <span>#Box Office</span></div>
       <p>The small-budget film ‘Hanuman Ansh’, a surprise box office success, is officially set for its worldwide Telugu release on October 9, 2026. This announcement follows the film’s strong impact among Hindi-speaking audiences, where it started slowly but picked up momentum to cross the Rs 400 crore mark globally. According to trade tracker Sacnilk, the film's worldwide gross collection has reached Rs 414.06 crore.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-04/hanuman-ansh-sets-worldwide-telugu-release-for-october-9-202.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The Telugu release details were confirmed by the makers of the ‘Kantara’ and ‘KGF’ franchises, and 'Salaar'. Hombale Films, named by Bollywood Hungama, is leading the release of the spiritual drama. The production house conveyed its excitement on Instagram, stating, “We are delighted to bring the much loved #HanumanAnsh in TELUGU, for audiences to witness its divine brilliance on the big screen across the world.” Bollywood Hungama also noted that the film is presented by Swambhu Media Network.</p><p>‘Hanuman Ansh’, written and directed by Vishal Chaturvedi, intricately narrates the life and spiritual legacy of Neem Karoli Baba. Shobhinav Satyaa and Chandan Anand portray the lead roles, with supporting performances from Nikhil Dubey, Udaysinh Rajput, and Purnima Tiwari. The film's spiritual story has resonated with audiences, enabling it to perform robustly despite its relatively modest production budget.</p><p>Detailed box office figures from Sacnilk indicate that on Day 56, 'Hanuman Ansh' collected Rs 2.90 crore net in India across 4,345 shows. Its total India gross collection stands at Rs 374.86 crore, with an India net collection of Rs 317.38 crore. Additionally, the film garnered Rs 10 lakh overseas on Day 56, contributing to its total overseas gross of Rs 39.20 crore. The production house is also actively involved in other major projects, including Prabhas’ ‘Salaar: Part 2 – Shouryaanga Parvam’, ‘Suriya 48’, and a forthcoming collaboration with Bollywood star Hrithik Roshan.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft effectively utilizes all source material, including specific box office figures and production house details, into a coherent report.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>How this was reported · 2 sources</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/telugu/movies/news/makers-of-kantara-kgf-salaar-to-bring-telugu-release-of-hanuman-ansh-worldwide-release-on-october-9/articleshow/134638084.cms" rel="noopener">TOI Entertainment</a></li><li><a href="https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/south-cinema/hombale-films-to-release-hanuman-ansh-in-telugu-on-october-9/" rel="noopener">Bollywood Hungama</a></li></ul>
      <p>Synthesised from 2 independent reports on the same event. Details are attributed to the outlet that carried them; nothing outside these sources is published.</p>
    </div>
       
