     <article class="story single" data-beat="sports">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPORTS</span> · NDTV Sports · 2026-10-04 · editor 6/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>India Clinches Historic Asian Games Women's Hockey Gold, Secures LA 2028 Olympic Berth</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Asian Games 2026</span> <span>#Women's Hockey</span> <span>#India</span> <span>#China</span></div>
       <p>India defeated China 1-0 in the Asian Games 2026 women's hockey final held in Aichi-Nagoya, securing the nation's 16th gold medal. This victory marks India's first women's hockey gold at the Asiad since 1982, ending a 44-year wait. The decisive and only goal of the match was scored by Lalremsiami Hmarzote in the 10th minute of the first quarter, an occasion that also marked her 200th game for India, according to NDTV Sports.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-04/india-clinches-historic-asian-games-womens-hockey-gold-secur.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>A pivotal moment in the match, described by NDTV Sports as a &quot;Gold-Defining Moment,&quot; occurred in the second quarter when China was awarded a penalty stroke. Veteran Indian goalkeeper Savita Punia made an &quot;incredible save,&quot; preserving India's 1-0 lead heading into half-time. In the third quarter, India's defense faced further pressure. An initial penalty stroke awarded to China after the ball appeared to touch Navneet Kaur's foot was overturned following a referral, resulting instead in a penalty corner. Captain Salima Tete then made a &quot;brilliant block&quot; from the penalty corner, though she appeared to hurt her hand in the process. China also attacked down the left with a powerful low shot that narrowly missed the target in the 12th minute of the third quarter.</p><p>India maintained their one-goal advantage into the final quarter. China intensified their attack, notably substituting their goalkeeper for an outfield player in the 12th minute of the fourth quarter in a bid for an all-out offense. Despite this, India's defense remained resolute, holding possession towards the corner to run down the clock and denying China many big chances in the final quarter. Savita Punia made another save in the 13th minute of Q4 after China fired a shot. India had a rare counter-attack chance but was denied by the Chinese defense.</p><p>This Asian Games triumph not only brings home the gold but also secures India direct qualification to the 2028 Olympics in Los Angeles. The Salima Tete-led side concluded a dominant tournament run with seven wins in seven matches, scoring a remarkable 69 goals while conceding just three. This stunning achievement, highlighted by NDTV Sports, caps a memorable year for Indian women's hockey, which also saw their best-ever fifth-place finish at a Women's Hockey World Cup earlier this year, defeating World No. 4 China in the final.</p><p>What to watch: India's preparations for the 2028 Los Angeles Olympics.</p>
       
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://sports.ndtv.com/hockey/india-vs-china-live-score-asian-games-2026-womens-hockey-final-ind-vs-chn-live-match-updates-aichi-nagoya-12129480#publisher=newsstand" rel="noopener">NDTV Sports</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
