       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · News18 World · 2026-10-04 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Injured Flydubai Captain Praised for Preventing Mid-Air Retaliation</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#world</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Flydubai Captain Smit Machchhar is being hailed for his composure after a co-pilot allegedly stabbed him during flight FZ1073 on September 30, 2026. Despite suffering serious injuries, the captain prevented passengers from attacking the restrained co-pilot, urging them to focus on stabilizing the aircraft. The flight, which plummeted 17,400 feet, was subsequently diverted to Tabuk, Saudi Arabia, where all 174 passengers landed safely.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-04/injured-flydubai-captain-praised-for-preventing-mid-air-reta.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Captain Machchhar underwent emergency surgery in Tabuk before being airlifted to Abu Dhabi for further recovery. Passenger Dr. Maya Peretz praised the captain’s leadership under extreme stress, noting his focus on passenger safety. Indian Ambassador Deepak Mittal confirmed the captain is currently stable and recovering.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes the events, the captain's actions, and the medical status provided in the source text.</p>
