     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-10-04 · editor 6/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Protests Against CEC Gyanesh Kumar Mount in Delhi and Mumbai; CJP Demands Resignation</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Gyanesh Kumar</span> <span>#CEC</span> <span>#Protests</span> <span>#CJP</span></div>
       <p>A significant protest movement has emerged against Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar, with demonstrations taking place in Mumbai and Delhi, according to India Today. In Mumbai, the Citizens Justice Party (CJP), led by founder Abhijeet Dipke, organized a gathering at Shivaji Park in Dadar. The CJP presented three primary demands: the resignation of CEC Gyanesh Kumar, the freezing of the 2025 electoral list, and complete transparency in the appointment of future election chiefs.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-04/protests-against-cec-gyanesh-kumar-mount-in-delhi-and-mumbai.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Large crowds, including youths and first-time voters from various parts of Maharashtra, converged at the iconic Mumbai venue, holding the national tricolour and placards. This occurred despite the absence of formal police permission, with security forces maintaining a heavy presence at the site. The CJP has announced plans for further agitations across six other cities, culminating in an indefinite demonstration at Jantar Mantar in New Delhi by late October.</p><p>Meanwhile, earlier demonstrations in the national capital saw Delhi Police detaining over 1,100 political and student activists, as reported by India Today. These protests in Delhi proceeded with the opposition defying curbs, highlighting the widespread nature of the movement against the Chief Election Commissioner.</p><p>What to watch: Planned indefinite demonstration at Jantar Mantar by late October.</p>
       
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.indiatoday.in/india/video/protests-against-cec-gyanesh-kumar-in-delhi-and-mumbai-cjp-demands-resignation-ytvd-3008240-2026-10-02?utm_source=rss" rel="noopener">India Today</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       <div class="cityguide"><b>City guide</b><p>More on <a href="https://bharatdn.com/city/mumbai/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Mumbai</a> - census 2011 population, live weather and air quality, local food and getaways.</p></div>
