     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-04 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Search Underway for Three Boys Swept Away at Visakhapatnam Beach</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>A search operation is underway for three 14-year-old boys who went missing at Rushikonda beach in Visakhapatnam on Friday, October 2, 2026. The students, part of a group from Madhurawada, were playing in the water when strong waves pulled them into deeper sections of the sea. Their companions raised an alarm, but initial rescue attempts by locals were unsuccessful.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-04/search-underway-for-three-boys-swept-away-at-visakhapatnam-b.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>City police, marine police, local swimmers, and a specialized scuba-diving team have been deployed to search the area. Commissioner of Police Shankhabrata Bagchi is personally monitoring the rescue efforts near the IT SEZ junction. Authorities continue to search for the missing youths, and further details are currently pending.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is concise, accurate, and captures all relevant details regarding the rescue operation and the victims' backgrounds as reported.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/cities/Visakhapatnam/three-boys-swept-away-at-visakhapatnams-rushikonda-beach-search-on/article71536893.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       <div class="cityguide"><b>City guide</b><p>More on <a href="https://bharatdn.com/city/visakhapatnam/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visakhapatnam</a> - census 2011 population, live weather and air quality, local food and getaways.</p></div>
