     <article class="story single" data-beat="education">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">EDUCATION</span> · Education (aggregate) · 2026-10-04 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>US Master's Degree Costs $100,000 Amid Job, H-1B Warnings</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#US education</span> <span>#Indian students</span> <span>#H-1B visa</span> <span>#Dhaval Patel</span></div>
       <p>US master's degrees are reported to cost $100,000, a significant financial commitment for students. Dhaval Patel has issued a warning to Indian students considering this path, highlighting potential difficulties, according to The Times of India.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-04/us-masters-degree-costs-100000-amid-job-h-1b-warnings.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Patel's advisory specifically points to challenges related to securing jobs post-graduation and navigating the H-1B visa process. These factors are critical considerations for Indian students planning to study in the United States.</p><p>The warning underscores the need for prospective students to carefully evaluate not only the high cost of education but also the subsequent employment and immigration hurdles they may face.</p><p>What to watch: Future policy changes impacting H-1B visas.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Concise and accurate reporting of the provided source summary.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.?oc=5&amp;hl=en-US&amp;gl=US&amp;ceid=US:en" rel="noopener">Education (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
